# ---- PneumoScan frontend (Node/React) ----
# node_modules is always regenerable from package-lock.json via `npm ci`.
# frontend/dist/ is the OPPOSITE: it must be committed, not ignored, since
# Streamlit Community Cloud's build environment is Python/pip only and
# cannot run `npm run build` itself -- the plan's Risk #1/#2. The blanket
# `dist/` rule above would otherwise silently swallow it.
app/pneumoscan_component/frontend/node_modules/
!app/pneumoscan_component/frontend/dist/
# Same trap, one directory deeper: the vendored three.js files that must be
# committed (public/ is their source, dist/ is Vite's copy) sit inside a
# path segment literally named `build/` (three.js's own release layout),
# which the blanket Python `build/` rule above silently matches even
# though `dist/` itself is negated -- git re-applies later patterns
# against already-negated paths per path segment, it doesn't cascade.
# Found live 2026-09-28: three.module.js/three.core.js were silently
# missing from a real commit (only OrbitControls.js, which isn't under a
# `build/` segment, made it through) -- would have broken the 3D viewer on
# a fresh clone or deployment despite working locally off-disk.
!app/pneumoscan_component/frontend/public/vendor/three/build/
!app/pneumoscan_component/frontend/dist/vendor/three/build/

